% A user and a co-signing service, the user alone after 90 days
%
% The Logical English twin of a Bitcoin spending policy, written by the
% Miniscript translator (InsurLE2/migration/miniscript). Who can spend the
% coin, when, and why: each rule is one spending path of the policy.
%
% Source: the Miniscript page
%         https://bitcoin.sipa.be/miniscript/
%
% The source, as written:
%     and(pk(key_user),or(99@pk(key_service),older(12960)))
%
% The source, laid out (keys and hashes by their role, <like this>):
%     and(
%       pk(<the user>),
%       or(99@pk(<the cosigning service>),older(12960)))
%
% The legend (role <- key or hash as written in the source):
%     the user              <- key_user
%     the cosigning service <- key_service
%
% What it says (the spending policy, by BIP 379's semantics):
%     all of these:
%       a signature by the user
%       any one of these:
%         a signature by the cosigning service
%         the coin at least 12960 blocks old (about 90 days; older(12960))
%
% The weights (like 99@) guide sipa's compiler towards the likelier paths;
% they do not change who can spend, and the twin leaves them out.
%
% Try it in Minsc (the policy compiled to Miniscript, Script and an address,
% in the browser): the document "the policy in Minsc" below.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base cosigning_service includes these resources:
    temporal.

the templates are:
    the coin can be spent.
    the coin was confirmed in block *a height*; scenario element.
    the spending transaction is in block *a height*; scenario element.
    the coin has been confirmed for *a number* blocks.
    the witness contains a signature by *a key*; scenario element.

the knowledge base cosigning_service includes:

the Miniscript page is published at "https://bitcoin.sipa.be/miniscript/".
the text of the Miniscript page is at "sources/sipa_miniscript.txt".

the policy in Minsc is published at "https://min.sc/#c=//%20A%20user%20and%20a%20co-signing%20service,%20the%20user%20alone%20after%2090%20days%0A//%20The%20Logical%20English%20twin's%20policy%20(InsurLE2/migration/miniscript).%0A$user%20=%20034717e21c064758996df901f1d7a39c9e348a42972c9fc948fc84403d7710d1cb;%20%20%20//%20the%20user%20(a%20test%20key:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20key)%0A$cosigning_service%20=%20020191eb77be97634004cb0fa44285d455ae325456cbe3288406b2576c316e5f53;%20%20%20//%20the%20cosigning%20service%20(a%20test%20key:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20key)%0A%0Aand(pk($user),or(pk($cosigning_service),older(12960)))%0A".

the Tape run of 2026-09-14 is published at "https://tape.rewindbitcoin.com/explorer/address/bcrt1qxdrkevkr3cgmghvwqsmhyv90ftm7gnr28tc3qq4pj3zg7upmemrqlxts62".
the text of the Tape run of 2026-09-14 is at "sources/cosigning_service.chain.json".

% The spending paths of the policy.
rule user_and_service with provenance the Miniscript page,
        confer "A user and a 2FA service need to sign off, but after 90 days the user alone is enough":
the coin can be spent if
    the witness contains a signature by the user
    and the witness contains a signature by the cosigning service
        or the coin has been confirmed for a number N blocks
            and N >= 12960.

% The age of the coin, which the relative timelocks (older) measure.
rule coin_age_in_blocks:
the coin has been confirmed for a number N blocks if
    the coin was confirmed in block a height H
    and the spending transaction is in block a height M
    and N = M - H.

scenario path_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 1 — the path needs: a coin 12960 blocks old, a signature by the user
    the witness contains a signature by the user.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 862960.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario path_1_without_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 1 without requirement 1 — the path needs: a coin 12960 blocks old, a signature by the user
    the witness contains a signature by the user.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 862959.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario path_1_without_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 1 without requirement 2 — the path needs: a coin 12960 blocks old, a signature by the user
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 862960.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario path_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 2 — the path needs: a signature by the cosigning service, a signature by the user
    the witness contains a signature by the cosigning service.
    the witness contains a signature by the user.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850000.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario path_2_without_1 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 2 without requirement 1 — the path needs: a signature by the cosigning service, a signature by the user
    the witness contains a signature by the user.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850000.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario path_2_without_2 is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path 2 without requirement 2 — the path needs: a signature by the cosigning service, a signature by the user
    the witness contains a signature by the cosigning service.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850000.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario no_witness is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % an empty witness
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850000.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario flip_now is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, no delay passed
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 850000.
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness contains a signature by the cosigning service", "add: the witness contains a signature by the user"]].

scenario flip_after_delays is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % nothing signed, every delay passed
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 862960.
    flip_spend expects changes [["add: the witness contains a signature by the user"]].

scenario lost_the_user is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of the user lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by the cosigning service.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 862960.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario lost_the_cosigning_service is, as stated in the flip analysis of the policy:
    % the key of the cosigning service lost, everything else given
    the witness contains a signature by the user.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 862960.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].
    flip_block expects changes [["remove: the coin was confirmed in block 850000"], ["remove: the spending transaction is in block 862960"], ["remove: the witness contains a signature by the user"]].

scenario chain_path_1 is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at the refusal of attempt path_1:
    % the chain refused the spend: non-BIP68-final
    the witness contains a signature by the user.
    the coin was confirmed in block 122322.
    the spending transaction is in block 122322.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario chain_path_1_without_1 is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at the refusal of attempt path_1_without_1:
    % the chain refused the spend: non-BIP68-final
    the coin was confirmed in block 122322.
    the spending transaction is in block 122322.
    spendable expects answers [].

scenario chain_path_2 is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at transaction 8e0328ac9360be92f3eee9f19c788fad8a1bad579949bf9d7bf037a2f72b66f5:
    % the chain accepted the spend: transaction 8e0328ac9360be92f3eee9f19c788fad8a1bad579949bf9d7bf037a2f72b66f5
    the witness contains a signature by the cosigning service.
    the witness contains a signature by the user.
    the coin was confirmed in block 122322.
    the spending transaction is in block 122322.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

scenario chain_path_2_without_2 is, as stated in the Tape run of 2026-09-14 at the refusal of attempt path_2_without_2:
    % the chain refused the spend: mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Script failed an OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY operation)
    the witness contains a signature by the cosigning service.
    the coin was confirmed in block 122322.
    the spending transaction is in block 122322.
    spendable expects answers [].

query spendable is:
    the coin can be spent.

query flip_spend is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        the coin can be spent.

query flip_block is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        it is not the case that the coin can be spent.

the view custody explainer is:
    the title is "Who can spend this coin: A user and a co-signing service, the user alone after 90 days".
    the case is a scenario, with the documents it is stated in.
    the facts about "the witness" are
        the witness contains a signature by a key.
    the facts about "the timelocks" are
        the coin was confirmed in block a height,
        the spending transaction is in block a height.
    the result is whether the coin can be spent.
    the result shows its reasons.
    the result shows its citations.
    the result can be flipped, as "What would let this coin be spent?".
    the flip keeps the coin was confirmed in block a height,
        the spending transaction is in block a height.

